{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794293031,"nonce":"j7ORS/CkQ4SuTh0SQcWNfUFJwvA=","title":"Per-node storage is about 3 KB inline, and the node maps keep their doubled capacity","message":"Heap measured on cn_demo (release-debug, MallocStackLogging, malloc_history -allBySize, 15 s after launch), live heap 50 MB, of which about 11 MB is per-node storage for roughly 2,000 nodes:\n\n- `RenderTree::render_nodes` (IndexMap\u003cLayoutNodeId, RenderNode\u003e): one 5.8 MB allocation from `collect_render_props_boxed`. `RenderNode` is 1592 bytes and `RenderProps` 1432, inline, mostly `Option` fields a node leaves unset. 5.8 MB / ~1.6 KB is ~3,600 slots, so about half the capacity is empty after growth.\n- taffy node storage through `LayoutTree::create_node`: one 5.3 MB allocation. `taffy::Style` is 560 bytes; taffy's per-node cache and layouts add the rest.\n- `keep_snapshots` clones `RenderProps` and the taffy style again into `base_styles` / `base_taffy_styles` for each node with class rules (0.5 MB).\n\nOptions: move rarely set props (filters, 3D, motion, clip, scroll, text extras) behind a `Box` so a plain div is small; shrink the maps after a full build, or reserve from the element count; store the base snapshot as a diff.","files":null}]}